{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הן קרבו ימיך למות", :translit "hen karvu yamekha lamut", :gloss "Behold, your days draw near to die"} {:he "הן לה' אלהיך השמים", :translit "hen la-Shem elohekha ha-shamayim", :gloss "Behold, to YHWH your God belong the heavens"} {:he "והן לא יאמינו לי", :translit "ve-hen lo ya'aminu li", :gloss "And they will not believe me"} {:he "יען לא האמנתם בי", :translit "ya'an lo he'emantem bi", :gloss "Because you did not believe in Me"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking הן at Deut 31:14 and Deut 10:14; measure-for-measure: Moses said הן about disbelief (Exod 4:1), so הן announces his death (Num 20:12)."}], :frame {:text "God tells Moses his death is near using the word הן (Deuteronomy 31:14). Moses had earlier used the same word הן in a declaration of God's greatness (Deuteronomy 10:14). The Ba'al HaTurim reads this as measure-for-measure: Moses once said הן והן לא יאמנו לי, 'And they will not believe me' (Exodus 4:1), expressing doubt; consequently God decreed יען לא האמנתם בי, 'Because you did not believe in Me' (Numbers 20:12). The recurrence of הן signals that measure.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 31:14" "Deuteronomy 10:14" "Exodus 4:1" "Numbers 20:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking הן at Deut 31:14 and Deut 10:14; measure-for-measure: Moses said הן about disbelief (Exod 4:1), so הן announces his death (Num 20:12).", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:40:35.537022624Z", :model "glm-5.2"}